✅ Array Basics
Definition: Array is a collection of elements of the same type stored in a single variable.
Fixed Size: Size is decided at creation and cannot change.
Indexing: Starts from 0 (first element) to length-1.

✅ Types
Single-Dimensional: int[] arr = new int[5];
Multi-Dimensional: int[][] arr = new int[3][3];

✅ Key Points
Access: arr[index]
Length: arr.length
Default Values: Numeric → 0, Boolean → false, Object → null.

✅ Advantages
Easy to store multiple values of same type.
Fast access using index.

✅ Limitations
Fixed size.
Cannot store different data types together.